  "id": "pressor-effect",
  "term": "pressor effect",
  "definition": "Pressor effect is the raising of arterial blood pressure, as described here for the increase in mean arterial pressure produced by angiotensin II. In this source, the effect is discussed in relation to central nervous system control involving L-type calcium channels and nitric oxide.",
